      {
        "text": "Jeannine Wisnosky Stehlin is a small business owner and nonprofit executive who served on the Culver City Cultural Affairs Commission from 2016 to 2024. She says she wants to make the city more affordable and address homelessness, as well as improve traffic safety.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Jeannine Wisnosky Stehlin is a small business owner and nonprofit executive who served on the Culver City Cultural Affairs Commission from 2016 to 2024.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She says she wants to make the city more affordable and address homelessness, as well as improve traffic safety.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She has criticized the city’s budget, saying officials are borrowing towards reserves and putting municipal parking structures up as collateral. She also called the city’s $16 million homelessness spending excessive for a small city. She proposes a lobbyist registry to publicly disclose who seeks to influence city decisions. Her campaign says she successfully advocated for a new four-way stop and crosswalk at Motor and Braddock in 2026.",
        "cites": [2, 3, 4, 11]
      }
    ]
